relapse of Hodgkin's disease</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>1998</year><volume>83</volume><fpage>560</fpage><lpage>565</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9690550</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/(SICI)1097-0142(19980801)83:3&#x0003c;560::AID-CNCR26&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-T</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Menard</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Besson</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Rince</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Lambotte</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Lazure</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Canioni</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Hermine</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Brousset</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Gaulard</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Rapha&#x000eb;l</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Larroche</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hodgkin lymphoma-associated hemophagocytic syndrome: a disorder strongly correlated with Epstein-Barr virus</article-title><source>Clin Infect Dis</source><year>2008</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>531</fpage><lpage>534</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18611160</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/590152</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>